      "text": "Given the equations:\n\\[\n2x + 7 = 3\n\\]\nand\n\\[\nbx - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( b \\) such that the solutions to these equations are the same. Let's start by solving the first equation for \\( x \\).\n\n1. Solve \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\):\n\\[\n2x + 7 = 3\n\\]\nSubtract 7 from both sides:\n\\[\n2x = 3 - 7\n\\]\n\\[\n2x = -4\n\\]\nDivide both sides by 2:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-4}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = -2\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the second equation to find \\( b \\).\n\n2. Substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\):\n\\[\nb(-2) - 10 = -2\n\\]\nDistribute \\( b \\):\n\\[\n-2b - 10 = -2\n\\]\nAdd 10 to both sides:\n\\[\n-2b = -2 + 10\n\\]\n\\[\n-2b = 8\n\\]\nDivide both sides by -2:\n\\[\nb = \\frac{8}{-2}\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -4\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( b \\) is \\(\\boxed{-4}\\).",
