    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We are given the system of equations:\n\\[\n2x + 7 = 3\n\\]\n\\[\nbx - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nFirst, we solve the first equation for \\( x \\). Start by isolating \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n2x + 7 = 3\n\\]\n\nSubtract 7 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n2x = 3 - 7\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2x = -4\n\\]\n\nDivide both sides by 2:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-4}{2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = -2\n\\]\n\nThe solution to the first equation is \\( x = -2 \\). This means that \\( x \\) must be the same for both equations. Let's substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the second equation and solve for \\( b \\):\n\n\\[\nbx - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( x = -2 \\):\n\n\\[\nb(-2) - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\n\\[\n-2b - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nAdd 10 to both sides:\n\n\\[\n-2b = -2 + 10\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-2b = 8\n\\]\n\nDivide both sides by -2:\n\n\\[\nb = \\frac{8}{-2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nb = -4\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( b \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-4}\n\\]",
